# Varun's Voting Guide, 2024 General Election, converted from the YAML source at
# github.com/vsanthanam/voting-guide (src/content/guides/2024-general/).
#
# Conversion decisions, where the source and the Oval model disagree:
#
#   1. Structure. The source is organized by level of government (federal, state,
#      city), not by electorate. Oval's ballot tree models electorates. Rather
#      than invent sub-ballots the author never wrote, each source jurisdiction
#      is a root ballot and the author's sections are kept as sections. District
#      scope ("Palo Alto", "Oakland Hills") is carried in subtitles as the
#      source does. An electorate-faithful tree is possible but is a different
#      guide; see the notes at the end of this file.
#
#   2. BART. The source lists BART District 7 under both San Francisco and
#      Oakland. Oval requires each contest to appear exactly once, so the three
#      BART contests are a sixth root ballot with an eligibility line. This is
#      the cross-cutting-district case the model anticipated.
#
#   3. Recalls. The model has no Recall entity yet (DATA_MODEL.md, resolved Q6).
#      The two Oakland recalls are written as measures, which is what the
#      source does too (kind: recall shares the measure fields). Noted inline.
#
#   4. Per-pick notes. The source attaches "if you must" to one mayoral pick.
#      Oval has no per-tier or per-stance note, so it is in the recommendation's
#      note. This was deferred deliberately in the model; here is the first
#      real case for it.
#
# Source fields that map directly: office -> contest title; area -> subtitle;
# kind single/multi/ranked -> single/multiple/ranked; seats -> multiple N;
# candidates -> campaigns; incumbent -> incumbent flag; party -> party ref;
# picks (each slot) -> one support line, any_of -> several refs on one line;
# avoid -> oppose; why -> justification; measure + title -> measure title +
# subtitle; position yes/no/none -> recommend yes/no/no-position;
# note -> note.

guide "Varun's Voting Guide"
election "2024 General Election"
date 2024-11-05

note:
  Written by Varun Santhanam. Designed for voters in select cities in the San
  Francisco Bay Area. Always double check the options written on your ballot.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- parties

party @dem "Democratic"
  abbreviation "D"
party @gop "Republican"
  abbreviation "R"
party @aip "American Independent"
  abbreviation "AIP"
party @green "Green"
  abbreviation "G"
party @pf "Peace and Freedom"
  abbreviation "PF"
party @lib "Libertarian"
  abbreviation "LIB"

# ------------------------------------------------------------- candidates
# Only people who appear in more than one contest.

candidate @adam-schiff "Adam Schiff"
  party @dem
candidate @steve-garvey "Steve Garvey"
  party @gop

