# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# On an electorate-faithful tree. The model's tree is about who sees what.
# A faithful version of this guide would be: root "United States" holding the
# President and both Senate contests and all state propositions (every reader
# sees those), with sub-ballots per city, and under each city further
# sub-ballots for its congressional, assembly, state senate, and supervisor
# districts. That is around twenty ballots instead of six, and it moves every
# House and legislative contest out of the "Federal" and "California" groupings
# the author chose. The author's organization is by level of government, which
# is how official sample ballots are also laid out. Reconciling the two is a
# renderer question (group by level, filter by electorate), not a data one, but
# it means a Section cannot today hold sub-ballots, which is what "House of
# Representatives, then one block per district" would need.
